## 🚀 Quick Start

### Prerequisites
- Node.js 18+
- Docker & Docker Compose
- PostgreSQL 14+
- Git

### Local Development Setup

```bash
# 1. Clone repository
git clone https://github.com/jroc-os/core.git
cd jroc-os

# 2. Install dependencies
npm install

# 3. Setup environment
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env with your config

# 4. Start services (PostgreSQL, Redis, API, Web)
docker-compose up -d

# 5. Run migrations
npm run db:migrate

# 6. Seed data
npm run db:seed

# 7. Start dev servers
npm run dev

# Frontend: http://localhost:3000
# API: http://localhost:4000
# GraphQL: http://localhost:4000/graphql
```

